Title: THE LAST TRANSMISSION
Credit: written by
Author: Sam Wasserman
Draft date: 7/18/2026

FADE IN:

EXT. COASTAL HIGHWAY - NIGHT

Rain hammers a lonely two-lane blacktop. A battered PICKUP TRUCK rounds the bend, one headlight out, wipers losing the fight.

INT. PICKUP TRUCK - NIGHT

MARA VANCE, late 30s, buzzed dark hair, an olive M-65 jacket two sizes too big, grips the wheel. On the bench seat: a TAPE RECORDER wrapped in a plastic bag.

The radio spits static. Then — a voice, buried in the noise.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
(filtered, broken)
...if anyone can hear this... the light on Point Bastion... it's still on...

Mara turns it up. Static swallows the voice. She slams the dash.

MARA
Come on. Come on.

EXT. POINT BASTION LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

The truck skids to a stop on a gravel turnout. Above, an old LIGHTHOUSE — dark. Dead. Mara steps out into the rain, flashlight in hand.

At the base of the tower, a rusted steel door hangs open, groaning on the wind.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - STAIRWELL - CONTINUOUS

Mara climbs the spiral stairs, flashlight beam sweeping over peeling paint and salt-rot. Her boots ring on the iron steps.

Halfway up, she stops. Listens.

Below her, faint — the steel door CLANGS shut.

MARA
(calling down)
Eli?

Silence. She keeps climbing, faster now.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - NIGHT

A round room of glass and rust. The great lamp sits cold. Sitting cross-legged beneath it: ELI TRAN, 40s, wire-rim glasses, a thrift-store cardigan over a HAM RADIO rig cannibalized into something stranger.

ELI
You brought the tapes.

MARA
You said it was still broadcasting.

Eli flips a switch. The rig hums. Dials glow amber.

ELI
Every night. Same time. Forty-one seconds.
(beat)
Tonight it said your name.

Mara unwraps the tape recorder. Her hands are shaking.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - LATER

The tape spools. Through the speaker, wind — then the RADIO VOICE, clearer now. It is unmistakably MARA'S OWN VOICE.

MARA (ON TAPE) (V.O.)
Don't light the lamp. Whatever he tells you — don't light the lamp.

Eli and Mara stare at each other. Outside the glass, far out to sea, a light blinks on. Then another. A dozen. A hundred.

ELI
(whisper)
They found us.

EXT. POINT BASTION LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

The dark tower stands against a sea now scattered with cold blue lights, closing in like a tide.

MARA (V.O.)
(pre-lap)
How long do we have?

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - NIGHT

Eli cranks a hand generator. Cables snake to the great lamp.

ELI
If I'm right? Until dawn.
(beat)
If I'm wrong, we never had any time at all.

Mara looks at the tape recorder. At the lamp. At the lights on the water.

She picks up the IGNITION LEVER.

MARA
Then let's be wrong together.

She pulls it. The great lamp EXPLODES with light —

SMASH CUT TO:

EXT. OPEN OCEAN - NIGHT

A single beam sweeps the black water. The blue lights, hundreds of them, all go dark at once.

Silence. Rain. And then, from everywhere and nowhere, the sound of a HUNDRED RADIOS tuning at once.

FADE OUT.

THE END